::ENG2_U04_L05_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG2.W.03] Finding: A district report found that the pre-order pilot reduced unwanted trays. Which sentence best integrates the source?{
=A. A district report found that the pre-order pilot reduced unwanted trays after staff prepared meals from student selections.#Correct. This sentence identifies the source and states the finding clearly.
~B. The report had stuff about trays.#Incorrect. This is vague and informal.
~C. Trays went down or whatever.#Incorrect. This is informal and unclear.
~D. The lunch thing was awesome.#Incorrect. This is opinion, not source integration.
}

::ENG2_U04_L05_GP_Q02::[MLA.ENG2.W.03] Which transition best adds a related second source?{
~A. However#Incorrect. This usually signals contrast.
=B. In addition#Correct. This transition adds related information.
~C. Instead#Incorrect. This signals replacement or contrast.
~D. Although#Incorrect. This introduces contrast or qualification.
}

::ENG2_U04_L05_GP_Q03::[MLA.ENG2.W.04] Draft: "The reminders were a big deal and fixed the form thing." Which revision best fits an academic audience?{
~A. The reminders were super awesome.#Incorrect. This is still informal.
~B. The form thing got fixed.#Incorrect. This is vague.
=C. The reminders improved the routine by helping more students complete the form consistently.#Correct. This revision is precise and audience-appropriate.
~D. Reminders are cool.#Incorrect. This is informal and unsupported.
}

::ENG2_U04_L05_GP_Q04::[MLA.ENG2.L.01] Which sentence is complete and clear?{
~A. Because the report found fewer unwanted trays.#Incorrect. This is a fragment.
~B. The report, fewer trays, selections.#Incorrect. This is not a complete sentence.
~C. When students forms.#Incorrect. This is incomplete.
=D. The report found fewer unwanted trays after staff used student selections to prepare meals.#Correct. This is complete and clear.
}

::ENG2_U04_L05_GP_Q05::[MLA.ENG2.W.03] Which sentence best explains why the evidence matters?{
~A. Evidence is evidence.#Incorrect. This does not explain the finding.
=B. This finding matters because it shows how pre-order forms changed meal preparation, which connects directly to waste reduction.#Correct. This explains the relationship between evidence and the research question.
~C. The report is there.#Incorrect. This is too vague.
~D. Lunch exists.#Incorrect. This does not explain the evidence.
}
